cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use milipoint-runs, please cite it as below."
title: "milipoint-runs: run-disjoint evaluation of the MiliPoint millimeter-wave radar dataset"
abstract: >-
  The released identification and keypoint splits of the MiliPoint radar dataset shuffle overlapping windows before
  dividing them, so most test windows share frames with training windows. Five participants recorded the workout in
  several runs; with one run held out, identification accuracy of the dataset authors' PointMLP on them falls from
  about 94% to 37-39%. milipoint-runs rebuilds the released splits exactly, measures the overlap, runs no-learning baselines and
  two networks under released, run-disjoint and participant-disjoint splits, and pins every reported number with
  tests.
type: software
authors:
